   148	Stateful cells are 15 runs (3 seeds × 5); the rest, 24. Haiku's Stateful needed a third
   149	parser version: the second still dropped the patches Haiku writes in Markdown
   150	(`**StateUpdate:**` followed by a code block) — 731 of 3,000 at T=200, in 7 of 15
   151	episodes — which an adversarial review found (§6, item 7). The cells above use the third,
   152	which accepts 2,998 of 3,000 responses at T=200 and 749 of 750 at T=50; of those, five are
   153	empty patches (`{}`, nothing to change), so 2,995 and 747 change the state. The three it
   154	does not accept contain no object at all.
